pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% DEFECT: `output EQUISATISFIABLE` is an unqualified claim, but `solx` removes
% every assignment agreeing with the logged solution on the preserved variables.
% Here that is the only solution class, so the core set — and hence the output
% formula below — is unsatisfiable while the input is satisfiable. Sibling of the
% `conclusion BOUNDS` defect above: `EQUIOPTIMAL` survives solution exclusion
% only because it prints the value below which nothing was removed, and
% `EQUIENUMERABLE` already refused outright.
f 1;
solx x1;
output EQUISATISFIABLE FILE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
